							</h3>
							<span class="inline-flex shrink-0 items-center rounded-full border border-[#7ED4B6] bg-[#AFE3D0] px-2.5 py-0.5 text-[12px] font-semibold text-[#0f2e26] dark:border-hairline dark:bg-canvas dark:text-ink">
								Impromptu
							</span>
						</div>

						<ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-body">
							<li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
								<span class="flex h-5 w-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#0f2e26] text-[11px] font-bold text-[#afe3d0] dark:bg-[#afe3d0] dark:text-[#0f2e26]">P</span>
								<span><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Point:</strong> State your clear main position in the first 10 seconds.</span>
							</li>
							<li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
								<span class="flex h-5 w-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#0f2e26] text-[11px] font-bold text-[#afe3d0] dark:bg-[#afe3d0] dark:text-[#0f2e26]">R</span>
								<span><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Reason:</strong> Explain the primary logic or cause behind your stance.</span>
							</li>
							<li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
								<span class="flex h-5 w-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#0f2e26] text-[11px] font-bold text-[#afe3d0] dark:bg-[#afe3d0] dark:text-[#0f2e26]">E</span>
								<span><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Example:</strong> Anchor your point with a concrete real-world story, statistic, or observation.</span>
							</li>
							<li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
								<span class="flex h-5 w-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#0f2e26] text-[11px] font-bold text-[#afe3d0] dark:bg-[#afe3d0] dark:text-[#0f2e26]">P</span>
								<span><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Point (Restated):</strong> Wrap up with a memorable closing line that echoes your opening thesis.</span>
							</li>
						</ul>
					</div>

					<p class="mt-4 rounded-md border border-hairline bg-canvas p-3 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-body">
						<strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Speaking pace tip:</strong> A comfortable 1-minute speech runs at roughly 120–150 words per minute—use our <a href="/speech-time-calculator/" class="font-medium text-[#0D9488] underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:text-ink dark:text-[#AFE3D0]">Speech Time Calculator</a> to practice pacing your delivery.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Card 2: The PEEL Framework -->
				<div class="flex flex-col justify-between rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-elevated p-5 sm:p-6 space-y-4">
					<div>
						<div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 border-b border-hairline pb-3">
							<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
								The PEEL Framework (Best for Academic Essays &amp; Debate Arguments)
							</h3>
							<span class="inline-flex shrink-0 items-center rounded-full border border-[#7ED4B6] bg-[#AFE3D0] px-2.5 py-0.5 text-[12px] font-semibold text-[#0f2e26] dark:border-hairline dark:bg-canvas dark:text-ink">
								Essays
							</span>
						</div>

						<ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-body">
							<li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
								<span class="flex h-5 w-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#0f2e26] text-[11px] font-bold text-[#afe3d0] dark:bg-[#afe3d0] dark:text-[#0f2e26]">P</span>
								<span><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Point:</strong> Open the paragraph with a focused topic sentence.</span>
							</li>
							<li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
								<span class="flex h-5 w-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#0f2e26] text-[11px] font-bold text-[#afe3d0] dark:bg-[#afe3d0] dark:text-[#0f2e26]">E</span>
								<span><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Evidence:</strong> Support the claim with data, research findings, or historical precedent.</span>
							</li>
							<li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
								<span class="flex h-5 w-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#0f2e26] text-[11px] font-bold text-[#afe3d0] dark:bg-[#afe3d0] dark:text-[#0f2e26]">E</span>
								<span><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Explanation:</strong> Analyze why that evidence proves your argument and address counter-perspectives.</span>
							</li>
							<li class="flex items-start gap-2.5">
								<span class="flex h-5 w-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-[#0f2e26] text-[11px] font-bold text-[#afe3d0] dark:bg-[#afe3d0] dark:text-[#0f2e26]">L</span>
								<span><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Link:</strong> Connect the insight back to your overall essay thesis or transition smoothly to the next point.</span>
							</li>
						</ul>
					</div>

					<p class="mt-4 rounded-md border border-hairline bg-canvas p-3 text-[13.5px] leading-relaxed text-body">
						<strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Formatting tip:</strong> A standard body paragraph spans 150–250 words; verify your target length with the <a href="/word-counter/" class="font-medium text-[#0D9488] underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:text-ink dark:text-[#AFE3D0]">Word Counter</a> and check equivalent page counts with the <a href="/words-to-pages/" class="font-medium text-[#0D9488] underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors hover:text-ink dark:text-[#AFE3D0]">Words to Pages Converter</a>.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
